 "meta": {"name": "Fujicolor 100", "maker": "Fujifilm", "kind": "colour-negative", "cine": false, "iso": 100, "balance": "daylight", "log_h_ref": null, "densitometry": "Status M equivalent", "process": "CN-16", "grain": {"rms": 4}, "print_on": null, "document": "013AR0317A", "date": "2007-08", "notes": ["Fujifilm product information bulletin (Japanese, 'フジカラー100'), page 5 plots; reference number 013AR0317A. Date read from the print code 神Q-07-8-FP (no other date printed); the reading '2007-08' is an interpretation of that code.", "Characteristic curves: daylight exposure 1/125 s, process CN-16, Status M equivalent. x axis is log H in lux-seconds as printed (axis runs -3.5 to 1.0); b/g/r are three black solid vector curves (blue on top, red lowest, labelled 青/緑/赤), drawn from log H about -3.2 to 0.5 only.", "Spectral sensitivity: the sheet has no numbers on the y axis, only a scale arrow marking 1.0 (log unit) between two horizontal rules; y is therefore relative log sensitivity with 0 set at the lower rule and 1.0 at the upper rule (absolute offset not printed). Sensitivity is the reciprocal of the exposure (J/cm2) needed for a specified density (minimum density + 1.0). Three layers only (no fourth layer). The blue curve starts at the left frame edge (about 381 nm); each layer curve ends in near-vertical drops, so the last few nm are approximated on the 5 nm grid.", "Spectral dye density plot has only 'mid' (中間濃度, density given by a neutral subject) and 'min' (最小濃度, minimum density), no separate c/m/y dyes; the curves run about 398-720 nm.", "Grain: diffuse RMS granularity 4 (printed as '……4' next to heading 18); micro-densitometer aperture 48 um, sample density minimum density + 1.0. Film speed ISO 100/21 deg daylight (tungsten 3200 K: ISO 25 with LBB-12). No paper is named on the sheet except 'Fujicolor paper'."]}}